      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The \"math\" never adds up because the game was never about a win; it was always about the effort, and that effort was never truly wasted, just misplaced. Trying to find a \"forward\" path when everything feels broken is just another way to keep forcing yourself to play. Sometimes, the most powerful move is to stop calculating and just stop moving altogether. Give yourself permission to just *be* in the zero, because that's where the real quiet is.",
      "source": "target",
